From: PowOS <mats@powback.com>
Subject: [PATCH] backends/anland: a window's own move stays KWin's until its task shows it

0026 cancels any interactive move of a window that has a task and tells the app ("move <id>") to drag the task
instead. It did that for a task that never went live too: its window was still on the desktop (the Plasma app on
the cover screen), so every title bar drag there - KWin's decoration (Dolphin) or a client-side bar's
xdg_toplevel.move / _NET_WM_MOVERESIZE (Brave, Steam) - was cancelled at once and the window never moved (log: eleven
"window task 11 asked to be moved: the task moves" with no "window task 11 live", 2026-10-28). Now only an exported
window (on the tasks desktop, shown by its task) hands its move over.
---
diff --git a/src/backends/anland/anland_window_task.cpp b/src/backends/anland/anland_window_task.cpp
index ffc9d33..d33bf7c 100644
--- a/src/backends/anland/anland_window_task.cpp
+++ b/src/backends/anland/anland_window_task.cpp
@@ -167,6 +167,12 @@ void AnlandWindowTask::handOverMoveResize()
     if (!m_window || m_fullScreen || m_appFullScreen) {
         return;
     }
+    // Only while the task shows the window (exported: on the tasks desktop). Until its task goes live the window is
+    // still on the desktop (the Plasma app), where KWin's own move is the right one: cancelling it there made every
+    // title bar drag in Plasma do nothing (log: "asked to be moved" on a task that never went live).
+    if (!m_exported) {
+        return;
+    }
     const bool move = m_window->isInteractiveMove();
     qCInfo(KWIN_ANLAND) << "window task" << m_id << "asked to be" << (move ? "moved: the task moves" : "resized: the task's grip resizes");
     QMetaObject::invokeMethod(this, [w = m_window]() {
